From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WNM: Fix MLO PMKSA cleanup and link-removal disconnect handling

MTK driver-managed MLO connections use MLD addresses in the PMKSA cache.
BTM disconnection cleanup must use that address to remove shared entries.

The Link Removal Imminent check also applies to driver-managed MLDs.
It skips the whole-station disconnection timer when the station has
more than one link.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
+++ b/src/ap/wnm_ap.c
@@ -891,13 +891,19 @@ static void set_disassoc_timer(struct ho
 			       int disassoc_timer)
 {
 	int timeout, beacon_int;
+	const u8 *pmksa_addr = sta->addr;
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (ap_sta_has_ml_rsn(hapd, sta))
+		pmksa_addr = sta->mld_info.common_info.mld_addr;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	/*
 	 * Prevent STA from reconnecting using cached PMKSA to force
 	 * full authentication with the authentication server (which may
 	 * decide to reject the connection),
 	 */
-	wpa_auth_pmksa_remove(hapd->wpa_auth, sta->addr);
+	wpa_auth_pmksa_remove(hapd->wpa_auth, pmksa_addr);
 
 	beacon_int = hapd->iconf->beacon_int;
 	if (beacon_int < 1)
@@ -1047,7 +1053,7 @@ int wnm_send_bss_tm_req(struct hostapd_d
 		 * 9.6.13.9 (BSS Transition Management Request frame format);
 		 * else schedule full disconnection.
 		 */
-		if (ap_sta_is_mld(hapd, sta) &&
+		if (ap_sta_has_ml_rsn(hapd, sta) &&
 		    (req_mode & WNM_BSS_TM_REQ_LINK_REMOVAL_IMMINENT)) {
 			int i;
 			unsigned int links = 0;
